==============================================================================
(e) HOW MUCH OF THE RANGE DOES THIS CLOSE?
==============================================================================
  UNIFORM MEASURE BOUND: for k1 > K* = 203.865, every core P has
     |E_w(P)| > 2/21, so a complete k1-gap survives inside S(P) outside the
     bad set -- supplier (3) holds, uniformly over all 495 cores.

  clustered-regime floor  : k1 > 13*max(P) >= 13*12 = 156
  so the FINITE RESIDUE is : 156 < k1 <= 203   (47 values of k1)
  per-core residue is smaller: the floor is 13*max(P), so a core with
  max(P) = 12 needs k1 > 156, but a core with smaller max needs less.

